From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:08:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 189/194] glm: TF_GLM_KV_SPLIT keeps prompt states: each rank
 its own latent rows (both int8 scale planes) and index keys

On top of 0186 (latent.scaleBytes): the snapshot plan keeps ceil(at / W) local rows of every split cache
(cuda_state.latHeld / ikHeld), the same bytes on every rank, so the device and host tiers keep and restore a
split state; the disk tier (LEARN) is refused. A prompt chunk's prefetch is reset at its first layer.
Test: cuda_kv8_snapshot_test.zig, split ownership poison-restore at W 2/4/6 for every rank.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
